      "content": "That \"thresholding\" idea is interesting, but I want to make sure we aren't being too aggressive with it. If we just hide it behind a threshold, it might look like we're gaming the math if they do a secondary check.\n\nCan you go deeper on the \"sensitivity analysis\" part? I want a recommendation on exactly how to frame the mathematical narrative so that when a reviewer looks at the 2% number, they immediately dismiss it as a statistical artifact rather than a biological reality. How do we present the context so the conclusion is unavoidable?",
